# ConX Dynamic Panel Rules

- This repository is private commercial software for ConX.
- Never add HACS support, public marketplace metadata, or an open-source license.
- Read `MOSHIKO_BUILD_SPEC.md` before implementing features.
- Keep the Home Assistant backend fully asynchronous.
- Use public Home Assistant APIs only.
- Never hard-code example entity IDs.
- Keep hardware-specific behavior in `adapters/`.
- The frontend must use the integration API and must not control mapped hardware entities directly.
- Draft edits must never modify hardware before Sync unless auto-sync is explicitly enabled.
- Every integration-generated relay change must use transition suppression.
- Add or update tests for every behavior change.
- Preserve stored profiles and applied snapshots during upgrades.
- Support English and Hebrew RTL in all user-facing UI.
- Do not store or execute arbitrary Python or untrusted templates.
- Before completion, run backend checks, frontend checks, tests, and production build.
